Z||000000||GT Bastard||02-16-2001||12:38 AM||||I'll start out by saying I was p*ssed... I had just spilled a three dollar Starbucks cappuccino all over my carpet after only taking two sips of it!  Someone had to die.  It's about 10:30pm and I pull up to a red light.  Instead of sitting on the brake, I'm working the clutch to stay still on the slight incline.  I hear a roar to my left, and there sits an 80's Mercury Marquis... A couple of 16-ish kids are in it mocking my plastic wonder.   His car looks tough... The brake calipers are painted red, and it's got chome wheels!  Oh my!  My hands are shaking whilst I wait for the light to go green. Suddenly, this 3.8 litre Sh*tbox embodies the hatred I feel for having spilled that cappuccino. I hear his tires squeal and he's jumped the light by about .5 seconds!  Luckily I have DUKE power.  I still beat him through the light and had a full car-length by the end of second gear.  Of course he kept on the throttle after I backed off(ricer blow-by.)  So there you have it.... Just close your eyes and let it soak-in for a second...... ahhhhhh, yeah baby.||||reg||11
Z||000001||frontal lobe||02-16-2001||12:52 AM||||Two questions:  When did South Dakota get a Starbucks???  Were you planning on pulling an all-nighter, or are you immune to the effects of caffeine???<P>I am glad for you there was someone there for you to take it out on.||||reg||1
