Z||000008||88formula||02-16-2001||05:49 PM||||Mercury Marquis chirp the tires you've got to be kidding. I drove one of those cars from New Hampshire to Massachusetts and that car is about the slowest piece of crap that I ever drove. It had throttle body fuel injection on a 3.8-liter v6 and got about 12 miles to the gallon because I was standing on the throttle to keep up with normal 75 mph traffic. I could peddle a bike from a stoplight faster off the line than that car could accelerate. <P>The Mercury Marquis with the 5.0 v8 engine though is decent for power. <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
